From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:06:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Guard: accept a ground claim where the server finds ground
 possible

From enforcing on sg1: a 1.7 player held in pre-game, walking off the
pedestal and pushed back onto it again and again, was kicked for NoFall,
"claims ground 3.2 blocks into a fall". A teleport resets neither the
client's onGround nor the server's fallDistance, so the client's answer to
the teleport - at the pedestal position 0.01 over the slab, still on the
ground as far as it knows - looked like ground claimed mid-fall.

The claim now stands, and is not flagged, wherever the guard's own idea of
the ground allows it: under the feet, an edge the box touches, floating
against a wall after a step, or the first move after a teleport. Mid-air,
where none of those hold, it is still refused and flagged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaGuard.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaGuard.java
index b7d9d30997be2631a65faa574f7ebd9710500fab..1246b85b6fa5899ddf628b5f474adf713f87e7bc 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaGuard.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaGuard.java
@@ -138,10 +138,15 @@ public final class AthenaGuard {
         if (!enabled || !movement || this.exempt() || !this.known) {
             return clientGround;
         }
-        if (clientGround && !this.groundSeen && this.player.fallDistance > 3.0F) {
+        // The claim stands where the server finds the ground at least possible: under the feet, on an
+        // edge the box touches, floating against a wall after a step, or just after a teleport, which
+        // leaves the client's onGround as it was (fallDistance is not reset by one either: a player
+        // pushed back onto a pedestal again and again keeps adding to it).
+        boolean plausible = this.groundSeen || this.groundStart;
+        if (clientGround && !plausible && this.player.fallDistance > 3.0F) {
             this.flag(6, "nofall", "claims ground %.1f blocks into a fall", this.player.fallDistance);
         }
-        return enforce ? this.groundSeen : clientGround;
+        return enforce ? this.groundSeen || clientGround && plausible : clientGround;
     }
 
     /** Positions are not the client's to decide from here on: a teleport, a respawn, a dismount. */
